# Build context control.
#
# The images need only package.json, tsconfig.json, src/ and hooks/ — but the
# Dockerfiles sit in fargate/ and build from the repo ROOT, so without this file
# Docker uploads the entire working tree to the daemon on every build. Measured
# on a real checkout: 2.5GB of context (terraform provider plugins 1.5G,
# harness/ 562M, benchmarks/ 95M) for an image whose useful payload is a few MB.
#
# This is not only slow. A large context is also a disclosure risk: everything
# here is readable by the build, and `results/` in particular holds full session
# dumps including file contents captured from real projects.

# --- heavy, never needed at build time ---
.git/
node_modules/
results/
terraform/
harness/
benchmarks/
logs/
docs/
*.zip

# --- secrets: must never enter a build context ---
openapi.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
!hooks/**
.claude/
.aws/

# --- local noise ---
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
selfhost/.env
